  "scope": "Exact existing-surface evidence fallback: the preserved source inventory contains 22 official-survey operation entries, exactly matching the immutable count. Shared executable bindings for the same provider method/path are merged into one normalized endpoint. The cited official html_reference artifact is retained as the v2 provenance root; no operation was inferred from a documentation crawl. Prior source-surface scope: Pass B full-surface expansion (re-verified against Smaily's live per-endpoint docs, not just the index page): the 5 legacy-parity read streams are unchanged (campaigns, segments, subscribers, templates, automations — segments retains legacy's exact api/segment.php call per the parity meta-rule even though that path is not a currently-documented endpoint, see the segments entry below), plus organization_users, segment_rules, segment_subscribers, and ab_tests read streams and 6 write actions covering subscriber/segment upsert, campaign-recipient unsubscribe, individual message send, automation-workflow triggering, and A/B test launch — the full documented mutation surface for Smaily's PHP API. Bulk contact-import/opt-in/forget/action-log/campaign-launch/campaign-and-ab-test-statistics endpoints are excluded as out_of_scope (breadth-vs-cost triage: statistics/logs are not syncable object streams, and launch/import/opt-in/forget are lower-priority mutations than the ones covered here) or destructive_admin where documented as an irreversible account-wide erasure.",
